equilibrium to the origin?" "$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[1,\\,1]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?"] [:db/cas 17592186431890 :question/worked-solution "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⇒\\,x=u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]x+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}](u+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]u+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}]u.\n$$" "To shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,⇒\\,x=u+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^