 in the last step, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A+I:$\n\n$$\n(A+I)w=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -8 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A+I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{2}$ of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ Recall that an *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nFirst, we compute $A+I:$\n\n$$\nA+I=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -8 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A+I:$\n\n$$\n(A+I)v=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}={{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A+I:$\n\n$$\n(A+I)w=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -8 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }{{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A+I\\,}{\\to }{{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A+I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\""] [:db/cas 17592186433720 :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}"] [:db/cas 17592186433721 :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}"] [:db/cas 17592186433722 :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\}" "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\}"] [:db/cas 17592186433723 :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}"] [:db/cas 17592186433724 :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\}" "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\}"] [:db/cas 17592186433725 :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}"] [:db/cas 17592186433726 :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}"] [:db/cas 17592186433727 :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\}" "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ \\,\\,1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\}"] [:db/cas 17592186433728 :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}" "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\}"] [:db/cas 17592186433729 :answer/value "B=\\{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}" "B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\}"] [:db/cas 17592186433730